claude: true
prompt: |
  Drain the Data-Coloured karr board. This is the ASCII/binary visualiser — a small
  pure-Perl distribution that renders a byte stream as ANSI-coloured text, with
  Data::Coloured holding the logic, DDC as a thin re-export alias and the ddc CLI
  script on top. Delegate behavior-relevant code to the data-coloured-worker agent and
  release audits to data-coloured-release-manager; follow
  .claude/rules/data-coloured-rules.md. Never release. Work that belongs to a
  sister repository is a ticket on that repo's board, not a local edit.
